    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21103" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hydrĭa</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδρία</span> (a water-pot;
		hence, in gen.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				jug</i>, <i>ewer</i>, <i>urn</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argenteae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 2, 19, § 47</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in hydriam sortes conicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 2, 51</span></i>
			, § 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">127: farris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sulp. Sever. Hist. Sacr. 1, 43</span></i>
			. Of the <i>cinerary urns</i> in tombs,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4546
			sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hydria</span></b> , <i>a
				comedy of Menander</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 11,
				3, 91</span></i>.</div>
